  "question": {
    "text": "A thin Plano-convex glass lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>.5</mo><mo>)</mo></math> has its plane surface silvered and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> is the radius of curvature of curved part, then which of the following ray diagram is true for an object placed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>?<br />\r(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is at a distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> from the lens)",
